      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Bishop Osie England, the town’s founder, bought Interocean City in 1934 and turned it into a prayer‑centered community.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        16,
        17
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.intercessioncityliveagain.org/tour",
      "category": "people",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "In 1939, Intercession City published 'The Defender of the Faith,' a 16‑page gospel magazine that reached over 32,000 readers across the U.S. and abroad.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        25
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.intercessioncityliveagain.org/tour",
      "category": "culture",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "October 1939 saw the opening of Intercession City Bible College, establishing a local institution for theological training.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        28
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.intercessioncityliveagain.org/tour",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Originally planned as a coast‑to‑coast canal resort, the developer ran out of money in the 1920s, halting the project.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
